From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herrie <Github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] browser-shell: use ACG names that actually exist

browser-shell.perm.json asks for a number of legacy access control
group names that nothing in the image defines:

WARNING: luneos-dev-image-1.0-r0 do_validate_ls2_acg: Found 17 group(s) used in client-permissions.d but not defined
'applications' being used in:
  browser-shell.perm.json
'media' being used in:
  browser-shell.perm.json
'settings.read' being used in:
  browser-shell.perm.json
'signals.all' being used in:
  browser-shell.perm.json
'system' being used in:
  browser-shell.perm.json

- 'applications' is dropped, application.operation is already requested
  next to it (sam declares application.operation/launcher/devmode).
- 'settings.read' becomes settings.query, which is what
  com.webos.settingsservice declares its read APIs under.
- 'media' becomes media.operation, which is what com.webos.media
  declares its playback APIs under.
- 'signals.all' and 'system' are dropped. Per browser-shell.role.json
  com.webos.chromium.memory* only talks to com.palm.bus and
  com.webos.service.memorymanager; hub signal subscription does not
  need an ACG and memorymanager.query covers the rest.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
Upstream-Status: Pending

 .../browser_shell/browser-shell.perm.json     | 14 ++++----------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/webos/install/browser_shell/browser-shell.perm.json b/src/webos/install/browser_shell/browser-shell.perm.json
index 6384df7569..bb083ae438 100644
--- a/src/webos/install/browser_shell/browser-shell.perm.json
+++ b/src/webos/install/browser_shell/browser-shell.perm.json
@@ -2,21 +2,15 @@
   "com.webos.app.enactbrowser*": [
     "application.operation",
     "application.launcher",
-    "applications",
-    "settings.read",
-    "signals.all"
+    "settings.query"
   ],
   "com.webos.app.test.browsershell*": [
-    "application.operation",
-    "applications"
+    "application.operation"
   ],
   "com.webos.settingsservice.client*": [
-    "settings.read",
     "settings.query"
   ],
   "com.webos.chromium.memory.*": [
-    "signals.all",
-    "system",
     "memorymanager.query"
   ],
   "com.webos.chromium.audio*": [
@@ -28,7 +22,7 @@
     "camera.operation"
   ],
   "com.webos.rm.client.*": [
-    "media"
+    "media.operation"
   ],
   "com.webos.chromium.installablemanager*": [
     "applicationinstall.management",
